# =============================================================================
# docker.list.chroot - Docker CE source used only WHILE BUILDING the image
# nimbus:docker.list.chroot
# =============================================================================
# What: Docker's official Trixie repository, from which live-build installs
#       the packages in package-lists/50-docker.list.chroot.
# Why:  Docker CE is not in Debian (spec Tab A). During the chroot stage
#       live-build writes this file as /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list and
#       trusts it through docker.key.chroot, which it copies to
#       /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/docker.key.chroot.asc. At the end of the chroot
#       stage live-build deletes both again and installs docker.list.binary
#       in their place (live-build 1:20250505, chroot_archives). So this
#       source deliberately has no signed-by option, and nothing from it
#       stays in the image (docs/PLAN.md NOTE-03). build/build.sh checks the
#       finished image for exactly that.
# Key:  docker.key.chroot is Docker's signing key, kept byte-identical to
#       Docker's download. Fingerprint:
#           9DC8 5822 9FC7 DD38 854A  E2D8 8D81 803C 0EBF CD88
#       Checked by build/build.sh, tools/build-debs.sh and CI
#       (tools/fetch-docker-key.sh --verify-local); refresh it with
#       tools/fetch-docker-key.sh.
# Tokens: @NIMBUS_*@ values are filled in from build/nimbus.conf by build.sh.
# =============================================================================
deb [arch=@NIMBUS_ARCH@] @NIMBUS_DOCKER_APT_URL@ @NIMBUS_DEBIAN_SUITE@ stable
